    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493312367/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """really must meet, you would like him so much - he has been tried five times for murder. He only resented it the last time, when they accused him of hiring “a nigger to kill a man - ‘as if I couldn’t do my killing myself!’ ”
Then B.B. and I hurried off to meet. Billy Taylor, such a nice lad of 21, and talk to him about his future, that agonizing subject to a boy of his age. Both Bernhard and I thought what a fine fellow he was, and what a good husband he would make for Ray - if ever! But Bernhard said it would be fatal for them to meet  now.
Monday Nov. 30. 1903. Hotel Somerset Boston 
B.B. went to the Museum, and I went with Mrs. Rogers to see her home for underpaid shop-girls, and its splendid matron, Miss Sarah """^^xsd:string ;
